<<<
certitude is now restricted to the single sense of absolute conviction or feeling quite sure; certainty can, but often does not, mean this also, _ & the use of c, may therefore obviate ambiguity. D3
===
**certitude** is now restricted to the single sense of absolute conviction or feeling quite sure; *certainty* can, but often does not, mean this also, & the use of *c.* may therefore obviate ambiguity.
>>>

